namtor (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the enrollment scan page freezing the app: the progress poll was
    registered inside the render it triggers, doubling every 500 ms.
  * Fix every error route dead-ending with no message and inert buttons.
  * Fix Back permanently breaking Enroll and leaking the camera session.
  * Surface polkit denials on PAM toggles instead of silently reverting.
  * Stop presenting invented values as measurements on the scan, review and
    System pages.
  * Report a daemon that dies mid-scan instead of freezing the numbers.
  * Wire the screen-reader announcement throttle; show a readable "last used"
    time; make the troubleshooting rows do something; load a real gettext
    catalog.

 -- finley <finley.laempe@math.uni-freiburg.de>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:32:20 +0200

namtor (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the PAM editor as `namtor pam-edit`. The install scripts and
    lifecycle.sh all drove a namtor-pam-edit binary that was never shipped, and
    lifecycle.sh warns and skips when it is missing — so PAM snapshot, migrate,
    disable-all and purge were all silent no-ops, and removing the package left
    pam_namtor.so entries behind in /etc/pam.d.
  * Refuse to enable a PAM service with no password fallback. The check
    classified the candidate stack, which already contained the namtor block,
    and the classifier returns Safe on seeing that block before it ever
    evaluates the fallback rule.
  * Refuse to write a PAM block for a pam_namtor.so that is not installed.
  * Add `namtor pam-edit restore` to revert a service from its verified backup.
  * Group resolution no longer takes its path from the environment.
  * Cover the no-TPM software-fallback path in the UI; wire up the three CI
    gates that nothing ran.

 -- finley <finley.laempe@math.uni-freiburg.de>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:28:09 +0200

namtor (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * One `namtor` multi-call binary replaces four separate executables
    (73.7 MB -> 26 MB). The worker remains a separate process via
    /proc/self/exe, so the sandbox boundary is unchanged.
  * The worker sandbox is now actually applied; it never had been.
  * The PAD radial gate abstains instead of vetoing frames it cannot
    assess. It had refused 23 of 24 genuine faces.

 -- finley <finley.laempe@math.uni-freiburg.de>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:19:49 +0200

namtor (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Single desktop UI: namtor-gnome renamed to namtor-ui, and the Plasma 6
    KCM (namtor-kde) removed. namtor-ui Provides/Replaces/Breaks both former
    names so an existing install migrates instead of file-conflicting.
  * Enrollment guidance is derived from real per-frame measurements
    (blur, illumination, pose, face size, saturation) instead of one
    fabricated scalar; all nine guidance messages are now reachable.
  * namtor-ui Depends: namtor (= 0.2.0-1).
  * Manual pages shipped on all three distros, including pam_namtor(8).

 -- finley <finley.laempe@math.uni-freiburg.de>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:13:03 +0200

namtor (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the namtor-gnome binary package to namtor-ui. It is the single,
    desktop-neutral GTK4/libadwaita UI with no GNOME-only runtime
    dependency, so the old name was the last desktop-specific artifact.
  * namtor-ui declares Provides/Replaces/Breaks: namtor-gnome. apt does not
    migrate a rename on its own, and both packages own exactly the same
    four files (/usr/bin/namtor-enroll-wizard, the .desktop, the metainfo
    and the icon), so without these the unpack fails on a file conflict and
    the old package lingers.
  * The install manifest now says package = "ui"; namtor-layout aliases the
    old "gnome" value, so uninstall and namtor-cli diagnostics keep working
    against a manifest installed before the rename.
  * namtor-ui Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-3).

 -- Nam-tor Project <namtor@example.invalid>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

namtor (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the namtor-kde binary package: the project consolidated on a
    single desktop-neutral GTK4/libadwaita UI, so the Plasma 6 KCM and
    its cmake/qt6-base-dev/libkf6*-dev build dependencies are gone.
  * namtor-gnome now declares Replaces/Breaks: namtor-kde. This is an
    upgrade-blocker fix, not tidiness: namtor-kde declared
    Depends: namtor (= <version>), so a leftover install of it would
    hold apt back from upgrading the core package.
  * namtor-gnome Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-2).

 -- Nam-tor Project <namtor@example.invalid>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

namtor (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split into namtor (core), namtor-gnome, namtor-kde binary packages.
  * Core: daemon, worker, CLI, PAM module, systemd units, sysusers,
    tmpfiles, D-Bus, polkit, manifests, bundled models + licence
    notices, lifecycle helper, SBOM. No GTK/Qt runtime deps.
  * namtor-gnome: GTK4/libadwaita wizard; Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-1).
  * namtor-kde: Plasma 6 KCM (Kirigami/Qt6); Depends: namtor (= 0.1.0-1).
  * PAM module at Debian multiarch path
    (/usr/lib/<triplet>/security/pam_namtor.so).
  * PAM remains OFF by default; remove keeps state, purge cleans all.
  * Models bundled from deterministic signed archive (no network fetch).

